IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ucta-nouns`
IMPORT `ucta-logic`
IMPORT `ucta-p1-goods`

-- Tests for ucta-p1-goods.l4 (sections 5 to 7).  Every expected value is written from the text.
-- The last argument of each section function is the reach of the section, computed in ucta-p1-introductory
-- and tested there; here it is given.


§ `s 5`

-- "when a person is using them, or has them in his possession for use, otherwise than exclusively for the purposes of a business"
#ASSERT `s 5(2)(a) the goods are in consumer use` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 5(2)(a) the goods are in consumer use` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 5(2)(b) the writing is a guarantee` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A writing with no promise or assurance of making defects good.
#ASSERT `s 5(2)(b) the writing is a guarantee` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not in writing.
#ASSERT `s 5(2)(b) the writing is a guarantee` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "does not apply as between the parties to a contract under or in pursuance of which possession or ownership of the goods passed"
#ASSERT `s 5(3) section 5 applies as between the parties` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 5(3) section 5 applies as between the parties` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- All of (a), (b), the type of goods, consumer use and a guarantee; subsection (3) is silent.
#ASSERT `s 5(1) the person can exclude or restrict liability for the loss or damage by a term or notice in a guarantee` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Subsection (3): not applicable as between the parties to the sale.
#ASSERT `s 5(1) the person can exclude or restrict liability for the loss or damage by a term or notice in a guarantee` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Goods not of a type ordinarily supplied for private use or consumption.
#ASSERT `s 5(1) the person can exclude or restrict liability for the loss or damage by a term or notice in a guarantee` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 5(1) the person can exclude or restrict liability for the loss or damage by a term or notice in a guarantee` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not in consumer use.
#ASSERT `s 5(1) the person can exclude or restrict liability for the loss or damage by a term or notice in a guarantee` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not arising from the goods proving defective.
#ASSERT `s 5(1) the person can exclude or restrict liability for the loss or damage by a term or notice in a guarantee` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not resulting from the negligence of a person concerned in the manufacture or distribution.
#ASSERT `s 5(1) the person can exclude or restrict liability for the loss or damage by a term or notice in a guarantee` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
-- The term or notice is not in or by reference to a guarantee.
#ASSERT `s 5(1) the person can exclude or restrict liability for the loss or damage by a term or notice in a guarantee` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) NOTHING `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 5(1) the person can exclude or restrict liability for the loss or damage by a term or notice in a guarantee` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING `An exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 5(1) the person can exclude or restrict liability for the loss or damage by a term or notice in a guarantee` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING `Whether an exception takes the section out of the case cannot be told` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 6`

#ASSERT `s 6(4) the liability is one referred to in section 6` TRUE `Another kind of contract` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Includes liabilities under any contract of sale of goods.
#ASSERT `s 6(4) the liability is one referred to in section 6` FALSE `A contract of sale of goods` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6(4) the liability is one referred to in section 6` FALSE `A hire-purchase agreement` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "include": the list is not closed (section 1(3) then confines sections 2 to 7 to business liability).
#ASSERT `s 6(4) the liability is one referred to in section 6` FALSE `Another kind of contract` EQUALS NOTHING
-- "cannot be excluded or restricted by reference to any contract term".
#ASSERT `s 6(1) the person can exclude or restrict liability for breach of the obligations arising from the title provisions` `Sale of Goods Act 1979 section 12` `A contract term` `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(1) the person can exclude or restrict liability for breach of the obligations arising from the title provisions` `Hire-Purchase Act 1969 section 6` `A contract term` `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Subsection (2)'s obligations, not (1)'s.
#ASSERT `s 6(1) the person can exclude or restrict liability for breach of the obligations arising from the title provisions` `Sale of Goods Act 1979 section 13, 14 or 15` `A contract term` `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6(1) the person can exclude or restrict liability for breach of the obligations arising from the title provisions` `Another obligation` `A contract term` `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Section 6 speaks of "any contract term", not of a notice.
#ASSERT `s 6(1) the person can exclude or restrict liability for breach of the obligations arising from the title provisions` `Sale of Goods Act 1979 section 12` `A notice that does not have contractual effect` `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6(1) the person can exclude or restrict liability for breach of the obligations arising from the title provisions` `Sale of Goods Act 1979 section 12` `A notice that has contractual effect` `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6(1) the person can exclude or restrict liability for breach of the obligations arising from the title provisions` `Sale of Goods Act 1979 section 12` `A contract term` `An exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6(1) the person can exclude or restrict liability for breach of the obligations arising from the title provisions` `Sale of Goods Act 1979 section 12` `A contract term` `Whether an exception takes the section out of the case cannot be told` EQUALS NOTHING
-- "As against a person dealing as consumer ... cannot be excluded or restricted by reference to any contract term".
#ASSERT `s 6(2) the person can exclude or restrict, as against a person dealing as consumer, liability for breach of the obligations arising from the quality provisions` (JUST TRUE) `Sale of Goods Act 1979 section 13, 14 or 15` `A contract term` `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(2) the person can exclude or restrict, as against a person dealing as consumer, liability for breach of the obligations arising from the quality provisions` (JUST TRUE) `Hire-Purchase Act 1969 section 6A, 6B or 6C` `A contract term` `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not a consumer: subsection (3) governs.
#ASSERT `s 6(2) the person can exclude or restrict, as against a person dealing as consumer, liability for breach of the obligations arising from the quality provisions` (JUST FALSE) `Sale of Goods Act 1979 section 13, 14 or 15` `A contract term` `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6(2) the person can exclude or restrict, as against a person dealing as consumer, liability for breach of the obligations arising from the quality provisions` NOTHING `Sale of Goods Act 1979 section 13, 14 or 15` `A contract term` `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6(2) the person can exclude or restrict, as against a person dealing as consumer, liability for breach of the obligations arising from the quality provisions` (JUST TRUE) `Sale of Goods Act 1979 section 12` `A contract term` `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6(2) the person can exclude or restrict, as against a person dealing as consumer, liability for breach of the obligations arising from the quality provisions` (JUST TRUE) `Sale of Goods Act 1979 section 13, 14 or 15` `A notice that does not have contractual effect` `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6(2) the person can exclude or restrict, as against a person dealing as consumer, liability for breach of the obligations arising from the quality provisions` (JUST TRUE) `Sale of Goods Act 1979 section 13, 14 or 15` `A contract term` `An exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6(3) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` (JUST FALSE) `Sale of Goods Act 1979 section 13, 14 or 15` `A contract term` `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6(3) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` (JUST FALSE) `Hire-Purchase Act 1969 section 6A, 6B or 6C` `A contract term` `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6(3) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` (JUST TRUE) `Sale of Goods Act 1979 section 13, 14 or 15` `A contract term` `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6(3) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` NOTHING `Sale of Goods Act 1979 section 13, 14 or 15` `A contract term` `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
-- "the liability specified in subsection (2)" only.
#ASSERT `s 6(3) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` (JUST FALSE) `Sale of Goods Act 1979 section 12` `A contract term` `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6(3) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` (JUST FALSE) `Sale of Goods Act 1979 section 13, 14 or 15` `A notice that does not have contractual effect` `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6(3) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` (JUST FALSE) `Sale of Goods Act 1979 section 13, 14 or 15` `A contract term` `An exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "can be excluded or restricted by reference to a contract term, but only in so far as the term satisfies the requirement of reasonableness": it does.
#ASSERT `s 6(3) the person can exclude or restrict, as against a person dealing otherwise than as consumer, the liability specified in subsection (2)` (JUST FALSE) `Sale of Goods Act 1979 section 13, 14 or 15` `A contract term` (JUST TRUE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- It does not.
#ASSERT `s 6(3) the person can exclude or restrict, as against a person dealing otherwise than as consumer, the liability specified in subsection (2)` (JUST FALSE) `Sale of Goods Act 1979 section 13, 14 or 15` `A contract term` (JUST FALSE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Reasonableness is not shown by anyone: it is for those claiming it to show it (s 11(5)), so the bar stands.
#ASSERT `s 6(3) the person can exclude or restrict, as against a person dealing otherwise than as consumer, the liability specified in subsection (2)` (JUST FALSE) `Sale of Goods Act 1979 section 13, 14 or 15` `A contract term` NOTHING `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A consumer: subsection (2) governs.
#ASSERT `s 6(3) the person can exclude or restrict, as against a person dealing otherwise than as consumer, the liability specified in subsection (2)` (JUST TRUE) `Sale of Goods Act 1979 section 13, 14 or 15` `A contract term` (JUST TRUE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 6(3) the person can exclude or restrict, as against a person dealing otherwise than as consumer, the liability specified in subsection (2)` (JUST FALSE) `Sale of Goods Act 1979 section 13, 14 or 15` `A contract term` (JUST TRUE) `An exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
-- A consumer: subsection (2), whether or not the term is reasonable.
#ASSERT `s 6(2) and (3) the person can exclude or restrict liability for breach of the obligations arising from the quality provisions` (JUST TRUE) `Sale of Goods Act 1979 section 13, 14 or 15` `A contract term` (JUST TRUE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not a consumer: subsection (3), and the term is reasonable.
#ASSERT `s 6(2) and (3) the person can exclude or restrict liability for breach of the obligations arising from the quality provisions` (JUST FALSE) `Sale of Goods Act 1979 section 13, 14 or 15` `A contract term` (JUST TRUE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6(2) and (3) the person can exclude or restrict liability for breach of the obligations arising from the quality provisions` (JUST FALSE) `Sale of Goods Act 1979 section 13, 14 or 15` `A contract term` (JUST FALSE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Consumer status unknown: both subsections say no for an unreasonable term.
#ASSERT `s 6(2) and (3) the person can exclude or restrict liability for breach of the obligations arising from the quality provisions` NOTHING `Sale of Goods Act 1979 section 13, 14 or 15` `A contract term` (JUST FALSE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Consumer status unknown and the term is reasonable: (2) says no and (3) says yes.
#ASSERT `s 6(2) and (3) the person can exclude or restrict liability for breach of the obligations arising from the quality provisions` NOTHING `Sale of Goods Act 1979 section 13, 14 or 15` `A contract term` (JUST TRUE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Consumer status unknown and reasonableness not shown: section 6(2) (a consumer) and section 6(3) (not shown reasonable) both say no.
#ASSERT `s 6(2) and (3) the person can exclude or restrict liability for breach of the obligations arising from the quality provisions` NOTHING `Sale of Goods Act 1979 section 13, 14 or 15` `A contract term` NOTHING `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(2) and (3) the person can exclude or restrict liability for breach of the obligations arising from the quality provisions` (JUST TRUE) `Sale of Goods Act 1979 section 13, 14 or 15` `A contract term` (JUST TRUE) `An exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 7`

#ASSERT `s 7(1) subsections (2) to (4) apply` `A contract, not of sale of goods or hire-purchase, under which possession or ownership of goods passes` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Governed by the law of sale of goods.
#ASSERT `s 7(1) subsections (2) to (4) apply` `A contract of sale of goods` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7(1) subsections (2) to (4) apply` `A hire-purchase agreement` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No goods pass.
#ASSERT `s 7(1) subsections (2) to (4) apply` `Another kind of contract` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "As against a person dealing as consumer, liability ... cannot be excluded or restricted by reference to any such term".
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the person can exclude or restrict, as against a person dealing as consumer, liability for the correspondence of the goods with description or sample, or their quality or fitness` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) `Correspondence of the goods with description or sample` `A contract term` `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the person can exclude or restrict, as against a person dealing as consumer, liability for the correspondence of the goods with description or sample, or their quality or fitness` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) `Quality or fitness of the goods for a particular purpose` `A contract term` `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Subsection (1) does not apply.
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the person can exclude or restrict, as against a person dealing as consumer, liability for the correspondence of the goods with description or sample, or their quality or fitness` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) `Correspondence of the goods with description or sample` `A contract term` `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not a consumer: subsection (3) governs.
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the person can exclude or restrict, as against a person dealing as consumer, liability for the correspondence of the goods with description or sample, or their quality or fitness` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) `Correspondence of the goods with description or sample` `A contract term` `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the person can exclude or restrict, as against a person dealing as consumer, liability for the correspondence of the goods with description or sample, or their quality or fitness` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING `Correspondence of the goods with description or sample` `A contract term` `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the person can exclude or restrict, as against a person dealing as consumer, liability for the correspondence of the goods with description or sample, or their quality or fitness` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) `Supply of Goods Act 1982 section 2 (implied terms about title)` `A contract term` `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the person can exclude or restrict, as against a person dealing as consumer, liability for the correspondence of the goods with description or sample, or their quality or fitness` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) `Correspondence of the goods with description or sample` `A notice that does not have contractual effect` `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7(2) the person can exclude or restrict, as against a person dealing as consumer, liability for the correspondence of the goods with description or sample, or their quality or fitness` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) `Correspondence of the goods with description or sample` `A contract term` `An exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7(3) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) `Correspondence of the goods with description or sample` `A contract term` `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7(3) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) `Quality or fitness of the goods for a particular purpose` `A contract term` `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7(3) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) `Correspondence of the goods with description or sample` `A contract term` `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7(3) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) `Correspondence of the goods with description or sample` `A contract term` `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7(3) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) `The right to transfer ownership of the goods, or give possession` `A contract term` `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7(3) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) `Correspondence of the goods with description or sample` `A contract term` `Whether an exception takes the section out of the case cannot be told` EQUALS NOTHING
-- "can be excluded or restricted by reference to such a term, but only in so far as the term satisfies the requirement of reasonableness": it does.
#ASSERT `s 7(3) the person can exclude or restrict, as against a person dealing otherwise than as consumer, the liability in subsection (2)` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) `Correspondence of the goods with description or sample` `A contract term` (JUST TRUE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- It does not.
#ASSERT `s 7(3) the person can exclude or restrict, as against a person dealing otherwise than as consumer, the liability in subsection (2)` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) `Correspondence of the goods with description or sample` `A contract term` (JUST FALSE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Reasonableness is not shown by anyone: it is for those claiming it to show it (s 11(5)), so the bar stands.
#ASSERT `s 7(3) the person can exclude or restrict, as against a person dealing otherwise than as consumer, the liability in subsection (2)` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) `Correspondence of the goods with description or sample` `A contract term` NOTHING `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7(3) the person can exclude or restrict, as against a person dealing otherwise than as consumer, the liability in subsection (2)` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) `Correspondence of the goods with description or sample` `A contract term` (JUST TRUE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7(2) and (3) the person can exclude or restrict liability for the correspondence of the goods with description or sample, or their quality or fitness` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) `Correspondence of the goods with description or sample` `A contract term` (JUST TRUE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7(2) and (3) the person can exclude or restrict liability for the correspondence of the goods with description or sample, or their quality or fitness` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) `Correspondence of the goods with description or sample` `A contract term` (JUST TRUE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7(2) and (3) the person can exclude or restrict liability for the correspondence of the goods with description or sample, or their quality or fitness` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) `Correspondence of the goods with description or sample` `A contract term` (JUST FALSE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Consumer status unknown, term unreasonable: both say no.
#ASSERT `s 7(2) and (3) the person can exclude or restrict liability for the correspondence of the goods with description or sample, or their quality or fitness` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING `Correspondence of the goods with description or sample` `A contract term` (JUST FALSE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7(2) and (3) the person can exclude or restrict liability for the correspondence of the goods with description or sample, or their quality or fitness` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING `Correspondence of the goods with description or sample` `A contract term` (JUST TRUE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7(2) and (3) the person can exclude or restrict liability for the correspondence of the goods with description or sample, or their quality or fitness` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING `Correspondence of the goods with description or sample` `A contract term` (JUST FALSE) `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
-- "cannot be excluded or restricted by reference to any such term".
#ASSERT `s 7(3A) the person can exclude or restrict liability for breach of the obligations arising under section 2 of the Supply of Goods Act 1982` (JUST TRUE) `Supply of Goods Act 1982 section 2 (implied terms about title)` `A contract term` `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7(3A) the person can exclude or restrict liability for breach of the obligations arising under section 2 of the Supply of Goods Act 1982` (JUST TRUE) `The right to transfer ownership of the goods, or give possession` `A contract term` `No exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS NOTHING
