§ `Item 1 of the fix round: a flat negative takes the section out of the case`

-- The twins are in the text's own polarity: out is the text's own no, JUST FALSE, and it comes before the scope limits.
#ASSERT `s 6(3) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` (JUST TRUE) `Sale of Goods Act 1979 section 13, 14 or 15` `A contract term` `An exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(3) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` (JUST FALSE) `Sale of Goods Act 1979 section 12` `A contract term` `An exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 6(3) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` (JUST FALSE) `Sale of Goods Act 1979 section 13, 14 or 15` `A contract term` `Whether an exception takes the section out of the case cannot be told` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7(3) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) `Correspondence of the goods with description or sample` `A contract term` `An exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7(3) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) `The right to transfer ownership of the goods, or give possession` `A contract term` `An exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7(4) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` (JUST TRUE) `The right to transfer ownership of the goods, or give possession` FALSE `A contract term` `An exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7(4) a requirement of reasonableness applies to the contract term` (JUST FALSE) `Correspondence of the goods with description or sample` TRUE `A notice that does not have contractual effect` `An exception takes the section out of the case` EQUALS JUST FALSE
